{"type":"message","id":"3ccaa9bd","parentId":"d4030544","timestamp":"2026-10-17T23:37:26.969Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. The bug was in `ledger/currency.py`: `to_cents` used `int(amount * 100)`, which truncates. Floating-point error meant `19.99 * 100` came out as `1998.999…` and became 1998. Likewise `0.29` became 28 and `4.35` became 434. I changed it to `round(amount * 100)`.\n\nAll 5 tests now pass, including `tests/test_report.py`.\n\n`round` on the float product is fine for normal two-decimal prices. If you ever pass amounts with more than two decimals, or need exact decimal handling, `Decimal(str(amount))` would be safer."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":207,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":31664,"totalTokens":31873,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":31664}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792280244336,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8gunWoTQPo1FocqrAMi","duration":2619.1971790000007,"ttft":2605.371586000001,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":31666,"nonMessageTokens":15717}}}
